    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't want a bridge. i don't want a new movement. that's just a way of clinging to something that isn't there anymore. if a symphony keeps playing after the resolution, it's just bad composition. it becomes messy, it loses its essence. there is something profound, almost sacred, about choosing the exact moment of perfection and then simply... ceasing. why is it so hard to accept that a beautiful thing can just be finished?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
